[{"category":"section","location":"#GenomicCoordinates","page":"Home","text":"Documentation for GenomicCoordinates.\n\nGenomicCoordinates is a Julia package for working with genomic coordinates. It provides:\n\nchr2int to convert chromosome names to Int for fast comparison and sorting.\nGenomicPosition to represent a single position on a chromosome.\nGenomicInterval to represent a closed interval on a chromosome, built on top of Intervals.jl.\nfind_intersections to efficiently find overlaps between two collections of intervals.","title":"GenomicCoordinates"},{"category":"section","location":"#Installation","page":"Home","text":"using Pkg\nPkg.add(\"GenomicCoordinates\")","title":"Installation"},{"category":"section","location":"#Quick-start","page":"Home","text":"using GenomicCoordinates\n\n# convert chromosome names to Int, for fast comparison and sorting\nchr2int(\"chrX\")\n23\n\n# define genomic intervals\ni1 = GenomicInterval(1,   0, 200)\ni2 = GenomicInterval(1, 201, 400)\ni3 = GenomicInterval(1, 401, 600)\n\ngene1 = GenomicInterval(1,  50,  70)\ngene2 = GenomicInterval(1, 150, 200)\ngene3 = GenomicInterval(1, 350, 400)\n\n# find, for each interval in the first vector, the indices of overlapping\n# intervals in the second vector\nGenomicCoordinates.find_intersections([i1, i2, i3], [gene1, gene2, gene3])\n3-element Vector{Vector{Int64}}:\n [1, 2]\n [3]\n []\n\nIntervals also support the standard comparisons and set operations from Intervals.jl, such as <, ==, in, and intersect:\n\nusing Intervals\n\ni1 < i2\ntrue\n\nGenomicPosition(1, 100) in i1\ntrue","title":"Quick start"},{"category":"section","location":"#API-reference","page":"Home","text":"","title":"API reference"},{"category":"module","location":"#GenomicCoordinates.GenomicCoordinates","page":"Home","text":"GenomicCoordinates\n\nA package for working with genomic coordinates. It provides:\n\nGenomicPosition, a single position on a chromosome.\nGenomicInterval, a closed interval on a chromosome, built on top of Intervals.jl.\nchr2int, for converting chromosome names to Int for fast comparison and sorting.\nfind_intersections, for efficiently finding overlaps between two collections of intervals.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenomicCoordinates.GenomicCoordinates"},{"category":"type","location":"#GenomicCoordinates.GenomicInterval","page":"Home","text":"GenomicInterval{C,P}\n\nA genomic interval.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenomicCoordinates.GenomicInterval"},{"category":"method","location":"#GenomicCoordinates.GenomicInterval-Union{Tuple{P}, Tuple{Any, P, P}} where P<:Integer","page":"Home","text":"GenomicInterval(chr, first::P, last::P)\n\nCreate a GenomicInterval with chromosome chr, start position first, and end position last.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenomicCoordinates.GenomicInterval"},{"category":"method","location":"#GenomicCoordinates.GenomicInterval-Union{Tuple{P}, Tuple{Any, P}} where P<:Integer","page":"Home","text":"GenomicInterval(chr, pos::P)\n\nCreate a single-position GenomicInterval on chromosome chr at position pos.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenomicCoordinates.GenomicInterval"},{"category":"type","location":"#GenomicCoordinates.GenomicPosition","page":"Home","text":"GenomicPosition{C,P}\n\nA genomic position.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenomicCoordinates.GenomicPosition"},{"category":"method","location":"#GenomicCoordinates.chr-Tuple{GenomicPosition}","page":"Home","text":"chr(p::GenomicPosition)\n\nReturn the chromosome of the genomic position p.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenomicCoordinates.chr"},{"category":"method","location":"#GenomicCoordinates.chr2int-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Home","text":"chr2int(chr)::Int\n\nConvert a chromosome name to an integer.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenomicCoordinates.chr2int"},{"category":"method","location":"#GenomicCoordinates.compare_for_inclusion_1in2-Union{Tuple{T2}, Tuple{T1}, Tuple{Intervals.Interval{T1, Intervals.Closed, Intervals.Closed}, Intervals.Interval{T2, Intervals.Closed, Intervals.Closed}}} where {T1, T2}","page":"Home","text":"compare_for_inclusion_1in2(i1::Interval, i2::Interval)\n\nCompare two intervals for inclusion. Returns -2 if i1 is before i2, 2 if i1 is after i2, -1 if i1 partially overlaps i2 at the beginning, 1 if i1 partially overlaps i2 at the end, and 0 if i1 is inside i2.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenomicCoordinates.compare_for_inclusion_1in2"},{"category":"method","location":"#GenomicCoordinates.compare_for_inclusion_2in1-Union{Tuple{T2}, Tuple{T1}, Tuple{Intervals.Interval{T1, Intervals.Closed, Intervals.Closed}, Intervals.Interval{T2, Intervals.Closed, Intervals.Closed}}} where {T1, T2}","page":"Home","text":"compare_for_inclusion_2in1(i1::Interval, i2::Interval)\n\nCompare two intervals for inclusion. Returns -2 if i1 is before i2, 2 if i1 is after i2, -1 if i2 partially overlaps i1 at the beginning, 1 if i2 partially overlaps i1 at the end, and 0 if i2 is inside i1.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenomicCoordinates.compare_for_inclusion_2in1"},{"category":"method","location":"#GenomicCoordinates.compare_for_overlap-Union{Tuple{T2}, Tuple{T1}, Tuple{Intervals.Interval{T1, Intervals.Closed, Intervals.Closed}, Intervals.Interval{T2, Intervals.Closed, Intervals.Closed}}} where {T1, T2}","page":"Home","text":"compare_for_overlap(i1::Interval, i2::Interval)\n\nCompare two intervals for overlap. Returns -1 if i1 is before i2,  1 if i1 is after i2, and 0 if they overlap.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenomicCoordinates.compare_for_overlap"},{"category":"method","location":"#GenomicCoordinates.find_intersections-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Home","text":"find_intersections(x, y)\n\nFind intersections between two arrays of intervals. \n\nReturns an array of arrays, where the i-th element contains the indices of intervals in y that intersect with the i-th interval in x.\n\nThe intervals in x and y do not need to be sorted. However the function will sort them internally, so for repeated calls it is more efficient to sort  them before calling this function.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenomicCoordinates.find_intersections"},{"category":"method","location":"#GenomicCoordinates.find_intersections-Tuple{Type{Vector{Bool}}, Any, Any}","page":"Home","text":"find_intersections(::Type{Vector{Bool}}, x, y)\n\nLike find_intersections, but return a Vector{Bool} where the i-th element indicates whether the i-th interval in x intersects with any interval in y.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenomicCoordinates.find_intersections"},{"category":"method","location":"#GenomicCoordinates.find_intersections-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{Type{Array{Vector{T}, 1}}, Any, Any}} where T<:Integer","page":"Home","text":"find_intersections(::Type{Vector{Vector{T}}}, x, y) where T <: Integer\n\nLike find_intersections, but return the indices as Vector{Vector{T}} instead of Vector{Vector{Int}}.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenomicCoordinates.find_intersections"},{"category":"method","location":"#GenomicCoordinates.find_intersections-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{Type{Vector{T}}, Any, Any}} where T<:Integer","page":"Home","text":"find_intersections(::Type{Vector{T}}, x, y) where T <: Integer\n\nLike find_intersections, but return a Vector{T} where the i-th element is the number of intervals in y that intersect with the i-th interval in x.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenomicCoordinates.find_intersections"},{"category":"method","location":"#GenomicCoordinates.pos-Tuple{GenomicPosition}","page":"Home","text":"pos(p::GenomicPosition)\n\nReturn the position (offset on the chromosome) of the genomic position p.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenomicCoordinates.pos"},{"category":"method","location":"#GenomicCoordinates.segment_length-Union{Tuple{Intervals.Interval{GenomicPosition{C, P}, L, R}}, Tuple{R}, Tuple{L}, Tuple{P}, Tuple{C}} where {C, P, L, R}","page":"Home","text":"segment_length(a::GenomicInterval{C,P})\n\nReturn the length of the genomic segment a.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GenomicCoordinates.segment_length"}]
